  "text": "A Sateesh Kumar Senior Data Scientist\n\nPh: 9490009909 | Email: satish009909@gmail.com\n\nProfessional Summary:\n\nHaving 7 Years of experience as a Senior Data Scientist with Analysis, Design, Development, Testing, Customization, Bug fixes, Enhancement, Support, and Implementation of various web, stand-alone, client-server enterprise applications using Python in various domains.\n\nExperienced with Generative AI, Machine learning, Deep learning, NLP, Rag Pipeline, Agents, Crew agents, Autogen Agents, Agentic AI, AWS Bedrock, Aws Agents, Aws knowledgebase\n\nExperienced with LLM Model to apply on NLP problem\n\nExperience in working with several python libraries including beautiful soup, NumPy,Pandas, matplotlib, SciPy, PyQt,TensorFlow, PyTorch\n\nProficient in Statistical Modelling and Machine Learning techniques (Linear, Logistics, Decision Trees, Random Forest, SVM, K - Nearest Neighbours, Bayesian, XGBoost).\n\nTechnical Skills:\n\nLanguages Python, SQL Python Framework Fastapi,Flask IDE’S/Tools PyCharm, VS code Databases MS SQL, Data Science Machine learning, Deep learning, NLP,LLM,Gen AI Web Services SOAP, REST Methodologies Agile Operating Systems Window, UNIX, Linux Databases MySQL,PostgreSQL Integration Tools Docker Scrum Methodologies Agile and waterfall\n\nExperience:\n\nProject 1: Pre-screen Calling Agent\n\nDesigned and deployed a GenAI-based Patient Pre-screening Agent that engaged patients via\n\nSMS/Email/Twilio integration, and auto-followed up with non-responders.\n\nLeveraged OpenAI LLM, LangChain, AWS Lambda, Claude 3.5 Haiku, Mistral 7B, RAGAS to automate patient eligibility checks and communication.\n\nResult: Increased patient response rates by 42% and reduced manual coordinator workload by 60%.\n\n\n\nProject 2: Question Identification System\n\nBuilt an AI-powered NLP pipeline to detect and eliminate duplicate questions across clinical trial studies, ensuring a clean and standardized knowledge base.\n\nImplemented RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) with FAISS vector database + OpenAI embeddings to enhance duplicate detection accuracy.\n\nLeveraged OpenAI LLM, LangChain, AWS Lambda, Claude 3.5 Haiku, Mistral 7B, RAGAS Project 3: Clinical Trial Adverse Event Classifier\n\nBuilt an NLP-driven ML pipeline (Logistic Regression, XGBoost, BERT) to classify patient-reported symptoms as Adverse Events vs. Non-Adverse Events .\n\nStandardized reports using MedDRA ontology, handled class imbalance, and engineered temporal/contextual features.\n\nMonitoring (KS Test, PSI) for drift detection and continuous retraining.\n\nProject 4: Automated Patient Condition Extraction from Clinical Conversations\n\nBuilt an NLP pipeline to classify doctor vs. patient speech in clinical conversations and extract medical conditions (NER + ICD-10 mapping) only from patient statements, auto-filling structured databases.\n\nUsed BERT, RoBERTa, DistilBERT,BioClinicalBERT / BlueBERT, ICD-10\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nUtilized Python libraries pandas, numPY\n\nFamiliar with JSON based REST Web Services and Amazon Web Services(AWS).\n\nImplemented RAG(Generative AI) to find the similar question in existing question bank\n\nUsed prompt engineering(LLM) to find the variance in the similar questions\n\nUsed LLM Model to identify medical condition\n\nUsed LLm Model to find start date and end date of medical condition\n\nDeveloped predictive models using Decision Tree, Random Forest and Naïve Bayes and regression techniques\n\nDeveloped a layer of applications modules over the Python - Pandas library, delivered various data frame visualization tools, Data wrangling and cleaning using Python Pandas.\n\nPerformed data cleaning and data processing using Python Data frames.\n\nExtensive experience in Text Analytics, developing different Statistical Machine Learning, Data Mining solutions to various business problems and generating Data. Visualizations using R, Python and Tableau\n\nDeveloped NLP models for Topic Extraction, Sentiment Analysis.\n\nWork with NLTK library to NLP data processing and finding the patterns.\n\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nResponsible for gathering requirements, system analysis, design, development, testing and deployment.\n\nUsed Pandas as an API to put the data as time series and tabular format for manipulation and retrieval of data.\n\nDeveloped features and enhancements Python data structure libraries such as NumPy and Pandas. Extensively used matplotlib for generating graphical representation of data.\n\nUtilized Python libraries like wxPython, NumPy, Twisted, PyQt, Web2py, Pygal, and Plot.ly.\n\nImplemented Garbage collection with Cpython to enhance the performance, by garbage collecting the older\n\nEducation Details :\n\nData Science From INSOFE - 2019 with 64%\n\nB.tech In Mechanical From VISIT -2014 with 77%\n\nInter MPC From Bavitha 2010 with 81%\n\nSSC From Sri Balaji High School- 2008 with 91% Address :\n\nH.NO: 2-4-94, VepuriGeri Mahabubnagar Telangana",
